    "reason": "While 産出 (sanshutsu) means 'production' or 'output' especially for natural resources or industrial goods, it is too narrow for the general English noun 'output'. 'Output' can also refer to computer output, audio output, or general results, for which 産出 is not natural. 出力 (shutsuryoku) is a more general and natural equivalent covering a wider range of 'output' meanings.",
